/T (marking and post-exam analytics. Functional requirements identified include exam and mock-type selection, subject/chapter configuration, study-material upload or AI research, AI-based question generation, a full CBT interface, scoring with optional negative marking, detailed explanations and test history. Non-functional requirements include responsiveness of the configuration screen, reliability of score calculation, portability across operating systems that support Python and Streamlit, and secure handling of the Gemini API key through environment variables. Constraints noted include the Gemini API's rate limits and token costs, and the roughly 15,000-character cap placed on extracted reference material. 3. Elaboration )
/E (marking and post-exam analytics. Functional requirements identified include exam and mock-type selection, subject/chapter configuration, study-material upload or AI research, AI-based question generation, a full CBT interface, scoring with optional negative marking, detailed explanations and test history. Non-functional requirements include responsiveness of the configuration screen, reliability of score calculation, portability across operating systems that support Python and Streamlit, and secure handling of the Gemini API key through environment variables. Constraints noted include the Gemini API's rate limits and token costs, and the roughly 15,000-character cap placed on extracted reference material. 3. Elaboration )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
