/T (Overall, security and quality aspects are integral to the development of a robust and efficient software module. Security measures such as authentication, encryption, input validation, and secure communication protect against potential threats and unauthorized access. Meanwhile, quality aspects such as maintainability, performance optimization, reliability, usability, and scalability contribute to the overall effectiveness and user experience of the module. By integrating these principles into the development process, organizations can ensure that their software modules meet high standards of security and quality, leading to long-term success and reliability in real-world applications. )
