4424 0 obj
<<
/Title (marking and post-exam analytics. Functional requirements identified include exam and mock-type selection, subject/chapter configuration, study-material upload or AI research, AI-based question generation, a full CBT interface, scoring with optional negative marking, detailed explanations and test history. Non-functional requirements include responsiveness of the configuration screen, reliability of score calculation, portability across operating systems that support Python and Streamlit, and secure handling of the Gemini API key through environment variables. Constraints noted include the Gemini API's rate limits and token costs, and the roughly 15,000-character cap placed on extracted reference material. 3. Elaboration)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4406 0 R
/Prev 4415 0 R
/Next 4416 0 R
>>
endobj
4425 0 obj
<<
/Title (After reviewing the full feature list against the available development time and the limitations of a single-user, local Streamlit deployment, several features were deliberately excluded from the current version. These include user registration and login, admin accounts, a cloud-hosted multi-user database, online payment, social login, live multiplayer examinations, webcam-based proctoring and advanced anti-cheating mechanisms. The features retained for this version are exam configuration, study-material processing, AI question generation, the CBT examination engine, scoring and analytics, and local SQLite- based test history. This scope reduction keeps the project deliverable within the academic timeline while still demonstrating the complete, realistic mock-test experience end to end.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4417 0 R
>>
endobj
