/Title (Coding standards play a crucial role in ensuring the maintainability, readability, and scalability of software projects. A well-defined coding standard helps developers write consistent, high quality code, reducing technical debt and improving collaboration. A code walkthrough process is an essential practice that enables developers to review, identify issues, and optimize code for efficiency and security. This document outlines the importance of coding standards, key best practices, and a structured code walkthrough process tailored for the platform. Objectives of Coding Standards The primary objectives of defining and adhering to coding standards include improving code readability, ensuring that the code is structured and formatted consistently for easier understanding and modification. It enhances maintainability by ensuring that properly documented and structured code simplifies debugging and future enhancements. Coding standards reduce bugs by minimizing common coding errors and enhancing reliability. Additionally, they ensure security and performance by helping prevent vulnerabilities and optimizing execution efficiency. Lastly, they facilitate team collaboration by enforcing a uniform coding style that ensures seamless teamwork among developers.)
/Dest [61 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4571 0 R
/Next 4584 0 R
>>
